WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.850
Hi! Which is bigger, three sevenths or five sevenths? What about one third and one fifth? Today we'll compare and order fractions.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:21.714
When the denominators are the same, the parts are the same size, so the bigger numerator is the bigger fraction. Five sevenths is bigger than three sevenths.

3
00:00:21.864 --> 00:00:30.042
When the numerators are the same, compare the denominators. The bigger the denominator, the more parts, so each part is smaller.

4
00:00:30.192 --> 00:00:38.346
One pizza shared by 3 people gives each person more than sharing by 5. So one third is bigger than one fifth.

5
00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:44.802
One half is bigger than one quarter, and one quarter is bigger than one eighth.

6
00:00:44.952 --> 00:00:51.570
Compare three quarters and five eighths. The denominators and numerators are both different.

7
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:58.338
Change three quarters into eighths: multiply top and bottom by 2 to get six eighths.

8
00:00:58.488 --> 00:01:04.650
Six eighths is bigger than five eighths, so three quarters is bigger than five eighths.

9
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:19.074
To order one half, three eighths and three quarters, change them to eighths: four, three and six eighths. From smallest: three eighths, one half, three quarters.

10
00:01:19.224 --> 00:01:27.810
Watch out! Some pupils see that 5 is bigger than 3 and say one fifth is bigger than one third. That's wrong!

11
00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:35.490
The denominator tells how many parts. Cut into 5 parts, each part is smaller than when cut into 3.

12
00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:40.314
So one fifth is smaller than one third.

13
00:01:40.464 --> 00:01:49.458
Your turn! Which is bigger, two ninths or four ninths? Pause and think.

14
00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:59.970
Same denominator, so compare numerators: 2 is less than 4, so two ninths is less than four ninths. Did you get it right?

15
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:09.114
Another one! Which is bigger, one quarter or one half? Pause and think.

16
00:02:09.264 --> 00:02:18.234
Same numerator: the bigger denominator is smaller. One quarter is less than one half. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:18.384 --> 00:02:27.666
Here's another! Which is bigger, two thirds or five sixths? Pause and think.

18
00:02:27.816 --> 00:02:34.986
Two thirds is four sixths, which is less than five sixths. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:35.136 --> 00:02:45.498
Here's another! Which is greatest: one sixth, one half or one tenth? Pause and think.

20
00:02:45.648 --> 00:02:53.898
All the numerators are 1, so the smallest denominator is greatest: one half. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:54.048 --> 00:03:05.178
Last one! Order three fifths, one fifth and four fifths from smallest to greatest. Pause and think.

22
00:03:05.328 --> 00:03:14.922
Same denominator, so order by numerator: one fifth, three fifths, four fifths. Did you get it right?

23
00:03:15.072 --> 00:03:27.042
Remember: with the same denominator, the bigger numerator wins. With the same numerator, the smaller denominator wins. With different denominators, make them the same first.

24
00:03:27.192 --> 00:03:32.106
Next time you share fruit, think about who gets more!

